# SYNTHETIC replay fixture. NOT real EQOA output: every message format here is ASSUMED.
# Format (ours): <ts seconds><TAB><raw line>. Lines starting with # are comments.
# Designed edge cases:
#  - fight 1: you + pet hits in the same second (ts +0.0 and +2.0); a legitimately repeated
#    identical line at +4.0 that MUST count twice (replay lines are distinct messages);
#    a miss, incoming damage to you and to pet, a death and an ignored xp line inside the fight.
#  - fight 2 starts exactly idle_timeout (8.0s) after fight 1's last damage -> new fight (>= rule);
#    it is a single hit: zero-duration fight (DPS uses 1.0s minimum).
#  - fight 3: two overlapping targets plus group member Bob (hidden unless show_group).
#  - fight 4/5: misses at +5 and +9 do NOT extend fight 4; the hit 10s later starts fight 5.
#  - unmatched lines: a tell, a guild message, a garbled line -> unmatched.log (3 lines).
# Expected results: fixtures/synthetic_combat.expected.json (computed by hand).
